nks Theon now wants to  claim the sea stone chair but Theon says  he wants to support Yara in her claim to  the throne of the Iron Islands it's not  clear how Theon could help because the  iron men respect strength and Theon is  not strong right now so we'll have to  see how that goes either way we've got a  king's mood coming an election of the  new ruler of the Ironborn Assurant Euron  both have awesome speeches in this  chapter of the book hopefully some of  that will make it into the show anyway  at Winterfell Ramsay tries to be  intimidating but OSHA brings the SAS  pointing out that while he may flee  people at least he doesn't eat them like  the thins do beyond the wall OSHA tries  to seduce Ramsay mere tactic she's used  before and for a moment it looks like  she might kill him but round he's  playing her he knows she helped trick  one escaped Winterfell before so he  kills her then keeps on peeling his  Apple the death of OSHA is further  evidence that the umbers giving Rickon  to Ramsay probably isn't part of any  northern conspiracy and if it is the  plans already going badly back at the  wall edie john torment pod Brienne and  Sansa have brunch Tommen takes a fancy  to Brienne which is adorable and then a  Bolton man arrives with a letter from  Ramsay demanding Sansa and threatening  all manner of violence and rape and  awfulness in the books this letter is  known as the pink letter it arrives  before John's death and there's lots of  mystery surrounding it like some readers  believe it was actually written by mance  rayder  who is still alive in the books but in  the show it seems more straightforward  it's pretty clear that the letter was  written by Ramsay and delivered by a  Bolton man so Sansa urges Jon to ride  south with the wildlings to save Rickon  and Winterfell the numbers aren't good  Ramsay apparently has 5000 men while  there are only 2,000 fighting wildlings  but it sounds suggests that they ask the  loyal northern houses for help so maybe